// Legacy redirect map — ported from feat/astro-migration vercel.json (485 entries)
// Corrections applied 2026-09-04:
//   - 13 stale /jewelry/[name-slug] destinations updated to live SKU-based URLs
//   - 2 query-param destinations (/collection?cat=) simplified to /collection
//   - /shop/:slug patterns → /archive (historical catalog, not /collection)
// Corrections applied 2026-09-05:
//   - /retailers → /contact restored (new site has no /retailers index page)
//   - 9 missing WP blog post slugs added → /blog
// Corrections applied 2026-09-17 — every destination was audited against the
// live routes, the products table and the blog_posts table; 84 entries pointed
// at URLs that 404:
//   - 9 product destinations still used SKU slugs (deriveSlug switched products
//     to name-derived slugs); repointed to the live slug, except in101 which no
//     longer exists as a product → /jewelry/necklaces
//   - 27 retailer aliases (per-location and per-domain variants) collapsed onto
//     the 13 slugs lib/data/retailers.ts actually defines; the 2 with no current
//     retailer → /contact
//   - 4 blog slugs are not in blog_posts at all → /blog
//   - /collection, /retailers, /press, /video-gallery are redirect targets with
//     no page behind them → /jewelry, /contact, /about-bez-ambar, /archive
// Corrections applied 2026-09-29 — the /journal bucket was emptied (Kevin:
// "the blog redirects should go to /blog/{slug} not /journal/"). 128 old WP
// keyword URLs (256 rules with their trailing-slash twins) pointed at /journal,
// which is NOT the editorial index — it is a client-side Curator.io Instagram
// embed with zero articles in its server HTML. /blog is the real index (132
// live posts). Nothing points at /journal any more.
//   - 48 sources matched a specific live post → /blog/<slug> (26 distinct posts)
//   - 80 sources had no post that actually covers their subject → /blog
// Only 2 of the 128 had a slug-equal post — the new blog's slugs were rewritten,
// so this was a per-URL subject match, not a mechanical one. City pages
// (/engagement-rings-boston), competitor names (/turgeon-raine,
// /international-diamond-center-*), single-piece product pages and numeric
// slugs (/552, /599) all go to the index deliberately: a wrong specific
// redirect is a worse signal than the index. Low-confidence matches were
// demoted to the index for the same reason.
// Guard: `node scripts/check-redirects.js` re-runs this validation.

